\DOC ORTHOGONAL_COMPONENTS_BYTES64_TAC

\TYPE {ORTHOGONAL_COMPONENTS_BYTES64_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Proves that two 64-bit memory components at offsets from a common base pointer
are orthogonal, closing the goal.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. Applied to a goal whose conclusion is
{orthogonal_components t u}, where {t} and {u} are both 64-byte-word components
addressed from the same base pointer (with or without an added constant
offset), it solves the goal:
{
   A ?- orthogonal_components t u
   ========================================  ORTHOGONAL_COMPONENTS_BYTES64_TAC
}
\noindent The assumptions are left untouched.

\FAILURE
Fails with a no-match error from an internal matching step when the two
components of the {orthogonal_components} conclusion are not 64-bit memory
components addressed from a base pointer — for instance other kinds of
component formers — and also when they are such memory components but based on
two different, unrelated base pointers.

\COMMENTS
All observed successful traces show only this goal-closing behaviour, on
conclusions of this single shape with no assumptions present.

\ENDDOC
